---* `counted` - Counted every event on the days checked
---* `sampled` - Checked a sample of the events on the days checked
---@alias posthog.insights.InsightDataCheckMethodEnum "counted"|"sampled"

---* `too_many_events` - The days checked hold too many events to count
---* `read_limit` - The check would read more data than it is allowed
---* `time_limit` - The check took longer than it is allowed
---* `memory_limit` - The check needed more memory than it is allowed
---* `too_few_sampled_events` - The sample has too few events to give a share
---* `filtered_by_traffic_type` - The insight already filters on traffic type
---* `hidden_property` - A property the check reads is hidden from you
---* `invalid_filter` - The project's internal and test users filter cannot run
---* `on_request` - The check would read a lot of data, so it runs only on request
---@alias posthog.insights.InsightDataCheckSkipReasonEnum "too_many_events"|"read_limit"|"time_limit"|"memory_limit"|"too_few_sampled_events"|"filtered_by_traffic_type"|"hidden_property"|"invalid_filter"|"on_request"

---For the bot traffic check, the bots and crawlers found most often, most affected first.
---@alias posthog.insights.InsightDataCheckTopBotsList string[]

---For the internal users check, the team emails whose events the project's internal and test users filter keeps, most affected first. Only emails the caller may see as the team's are matched. Empty for a token without the `person:read` scope.
---@alias posthog.insights.InsightDataCheckTopEmailsList string[]

---The event names the check found most often, most affected first.
---@alias posthog.insights.InsightDataCheckTopEventsList string[]

---For the local development check, the local hosts whose events the project's internal and test users filter keeps, most affected first.
---@alias posthog.insights.InsightDataCheckTopHostsList string[]

---@class posthog.insights.InsightDataChecks
---@field status posthog.insights.InsightDataChecksStatusEnum The worst result across the checks. `no_events` when no event matches the insight's events, filters and date range. `unsupported` when the insight has no event series to check, such as a SQL insight, and when a property the checks read is hidden from the caller. `inconclusive` when no check could run. `partial` when some checks could not run and the others found nothing. `on_request` when the checks would read a lot of data for a quick check, so they did not run: send `depth` `full` to run them. * `passed` - No data issues found * `warning` - A check found a small issue * `problem` - A check found a large issue * `partial` - Some checks could not run, and the others found no issue * `on_request` - The checks would read a lot of data, so they run only on request * `no_events` - No events to check * `unsupported` - This kind of insight cannot be checked * `inconclusive` - No check could run
---@field checks posthog.insights.InsightDataChecksChecksList Every check, in a fixed order, whatever its result.
---@field coverage posthog.insights.InsightDataChecksCoverage|distilled.Null Which days and how many events the checks read. Null when the checks could not choose the days to read, such as for an `unsupported` insight.

---Every check, in a fixed order, whatever its result.
---@alias posthog.insights.InsightDataChecksChecksList posthog.insights.InsightDataCheck[]

---@class posthog.insights.InsightDataChecksCoverage
---@field date_from string The first day of the insight's date range.
---@field date_to string The last day of the insight's date range.
---@field days_in_range number How many days the insight's date range holds.
---@field checked_date_from string The first day the checks read.
---@field checked_date_to string The last day the checks read.
---@field days_checked number How many days the checks read. The checks read the newest days of the range, up to 7.
---@field filters_test_accounts boolean True when the insight filters out the project's internal and test users.
---@field events_checked number|distilled.Null How many events the insight reads on the days checked. Counted exactly, or scaled up from the sample when the days hold too many events to count. Null when neither ran.
---@field sample posthog.insights.InsightDataChecksSample|distilled.Null The sample the bot and duplicate checks read. Null when the sample did not run.

---* `quick` - Read within a small budget, so the checks can run on every load
---* `full` - Read with the same limits as the insight's own query
---@alias posthog.insights.InsightDataChecksDepthEnum "quick"|"full"

---@class posthog.insights.InsightDataChecksSample
---@field rate number The share of the events on the days checked that the sample read, from 0 to 1.
---@field events number How many events the sample read.
---@field distinct_ids number How many distinct IDs sent the events the sample read.

---* `passed` - No data issues found
---* `warning` - A check found a small issue
---* `problem` - A check found a large issue
---* `partial` - Some checks could not run, and the others found no issue
---* `on_request` - The checks would read a lot of data, so they run only on request
---* `no_events` - No events to check
---* `unsupported` - This kind of insight cannot be checked
---* `inconclusive` - No check could run
---@alias posthog.insights.InsightDataChecksStatusEnum "passed"|"warning"|"problem"|"partial"|"on_request"|"no_events"|"unsupported"|"inconclusive"

